    "title": "Iowa men’s basketball takes down Clemson in NCAA tournament, 67-61",
    "text": "by: Evan Denton Posted: Mar 20, 2026 / 10:05 PM CDT Updated: Mar 20, 2026 / 10:58 PM CDT After missing the two previous NCAA tournaments, the Iowa men’s basketball team came out strong in its opening game against Clemson. The Hawkeyes earned a hard-fought victory, 67-61, over the Tigers. Early on, Iowa’s defense was relentless. The Hawkeyes jumped out to an early 20-10 lead and never looked back. The win is Iowa’s first NCAAA tournament win since 2021. On offense, Iowa used a balanced attack to take down a tough Clemson defense. In total, three Hawkeyes scored in double-digits, including Bennett Stirtz’s game-high 16 points. The spark plug, however, was Alvaro Folgueiras. He added 14 points and four rebounds in just 20 minutes off of the bench. Overall, Iowa imposed its will on the glass. The Hawkeyes out rebounded the Tigers, 40-27. On top of that, Iowa made 24-31 free throws compared to Clemson’s 8-12. The win is a monumental moment in Ben McCollum’s first year as head coach. The Hawkeyes will look to book a spot in the Sweet 16 when they play the winner of Florida/Prairie View A&M on Sunday. Hawkeye Headquarters is presented by Veterans Choice Contracting LLC, your premier roofing and exterior improvement contractor. For more Hawkeyes coverage, follow @HawkeyeHQ on Twitter and Facebook. You can find Hawkeye Headquarters at HawkeyeHQ.com all season.",
